@echo off
rem Every MIDI controller, parameter and pitch bend of every patch of Spitfire Symphony Orchestra,
rem in the background.
rem
rem Double-click this file. It starts a MuseScore of its own with no window, like
rem "Extract SSO in background.bat" (MuseScore --extract-library ... --extract-controllers
rem --extract-pitch-bend, mscore/musescore.cpp): all 700 patches, one after the other, in one
rem Kontakt instance, at below-normal priority. On each patch it plays a note while it sets every
rem MIDI controller (0-119, channel pressure, pitch bend) to 0 and to 127 and listens to what
rem changes (level, brightness, balance, Kontakt's parameters), finds its own value again, tries the
rem parameters no controller moves, and measures how far pitch bend bends the note. It plays offline,
rem as fast as Kontakt renders (no sound comes out and no window opens), so it takes hours, not days.
rem It leaves the MuseScore you work in alone: its setups are the extract's copy, it opens no
rem audio or MIDI device. Only one background run at a time.
rem
rem Progress: Documents\MuseScore Sound Library Check\background extract.log
rem If Kontakt crashes or hangs on a patch, a new MuseScore goes on without that patch (the log
rem names it); each such round writes its own zip.
rem When it is done, that folder opens; hand back all the "... extract <date>.zip" files of the run.
rem To stop it: Task Manager, end both @MSCORE_OUTPUT_NAME@.exe without a window (the one that
rem started first, then the other).

start "" "%~dp0@MSCORE_OUTPUT_NAME@.exe" --extract-library "Spitfire Symphony Orchestra" --extract-patches all --extract-controllers --extract-pitch-bend

echo The measurement runs in the background (all patches of Spitfire Symphony Orchestra).
echo Progress: %USERPROFILE%\Documents\MuseScore Sound Library Check\background extract.log
echo That folder opens when it is done. You can close this window and keep working.
timeout /t 15
